// Sierra Training tab — renderer (SkyReach, Session 93; Phase 2 SkySierra,
// Session 94). Phases 1 + 2 of docs/sierra_training_tab_scope.md: the review
// queue + gap miner, and the GUIDANCE layer (sierra_guidance — short response
// directives cpl-chat v25 appends to every system prompt; the same-minute
// tuning knob that needs no redeploy).
//
// STATIC consumer asset (NOT regenerated by excel_to_dashboard.py), lazy-loaded
// by the inline boot in the tab shell on first activation of #tab-sierra-training.
//
// The improvement loop's working surface: every Sierra turn is logged
// (chat_interactions) and every answer is rateable (sierra_feedback) — this tab
// is where a TEAM MEMBER (not a Claude session) sees the gaps and drains the
// queue. Two panes, both server-gated by the reviewer/team-phrase RLS SELECT
// policies (the map_users.js pattern — a logged-out visitor simply gets no
// rows and sees the sign-in gate):
//   • FEEDBACK QUEUE — sierra_feedback newest-first; filters rating / audience /
//     page / status / has-note; rows expand to the full Q + A + note; a triage
//     status (new → triaged → addressed) advances via the SECURITY DEFINER RPC
//     sierra_feedback_set_status (reviewer/team-phrase gated server-side).
//   • GAP MINER — chat_interactions classified client-side: LOW-SIMILARITY
//     turns (top_similarity < 0.55 or null — the RAG corpus had nothing close:
//     the single best "what artifact is missing" signal), PUNTS (Sierra
//     explicitly said she didn't have it), recurring THEMES (keyword counts
//     over the gap rows), and an audience slice so student-facing gaps rank
//     first.
//
// GOVERNANCE (from the scope doc): this tab reads logs and triages feedback.
// It must NEVER write to the public cpl-knowledge-base repo — Sierra-corpus
// ingestion is Phase 3, and public-KB publishing stays behind its human-gated
// CURATION.md pipeline regardless.
//
// Self-contained behind the CONFIG block; scoped CSS injected from JS so both
// HTMLs are covered without a Rule-4 mirror.
